WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:07.140
It would feel reassuring to know exactly how things will turn out.

2
00:00:07.140 --> 00:00:14.012
Will the interview go well? Will they like my idea? Am I making the right

3
00:00:14.012 --> 00:00:14.470
choice?

4
00:00:14.470 --> 00:00:20.910
Preparation can help. But some answers only become available after we take a

5
00:00:20.910 --> 00:00:21.406
step.

6
00:00:21.826 --> 00:00:27.907
Making room for uncertainty means recognizing the limits of what you can know

7
00:00:27.907 --> 00:00:30.246
while still taking sensible precautions.

8
00:00:30.246 --> 00:00:35.919
Imagine preparing for an interview. You review the role, practice a few

9
00:00:35.919 --> 00:00:38.756
answers, and check the meeting time.

10
00:00:38.756 --> 00:00:42.150
You still can’t know every question in advance.

11
00:00:42.570 --> 00:00:47.470
At that point, more checking may stop adding useful information.

12
00:00:47.470 --> 00:00:53.738
You might try: ‘I don’t know exactly how this will go. I can prepare

13
00:00:53.738 --> 00:00:56.425
reasonably and respond as I go.’

14
00:00:56.845 --> 00:01:02.590
Choose a small, everyday situation where the risks are manageable. Ask what

15
00:01:02.590 --> 00:01:08.336
information you need for a reasonable decision—and what would be an impossible

16
00:01:08.336 --> 00:01:08.815
guarantee.

17
00:01:08.815 --> 00:01:12.556
You don’t have to feel completely comfortable before deciding.

18
00:01:12.976 --> 00:01:18.057
If repeated checking or asking for reassurance feels distressing or difficult

19
00:01:18.057 --> 00:01:20.828
to control, professional support can help.

20
00:01:20.828 --> 00:01:27.755
For today, leave a little space for ‘I don’t know yet.’ A reasonable next step

21
00:01:27.755 --> 00:01:29.602
can still be available.
